### Mobile app sign-up / login against the Identity service.
### In Development the code is also returned as "devOtp" (and always written to the log when email isn't set up).

@id = http://localhost:5001
@email = test.user@example.com
@password = Passw0rd!x
@scope = openid profile auctionApp IdentityServerApi offline_access

### 1. Sign up (username is made from the first name: "Test User" -> "test", "test2", ...)
POST {{id}}/api/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "phoneNumber": "+919876543210",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "acceptTerms": true
}

### 2. Log in with email + password.
###    Trusted device (device_token from step 3) -> tokens. Otherwise -> 400 with code OTP_REQUIRED + challengeId.
POST {{id}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=bmw_password&client_id=mobileApp&scope={{scope}}&username={{email}}&password={{password}}&device_id=my-phone

### 3. Enter the emailed code. remember_device=true also returns "deviceToken" (skip the code for 30 days).
POST {{id}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=bmw_otp&client_id=mobileApp&scope={{scope}}&challenge_id=PASTE_CHALLENGE_ID&otp=123456&device_id=my-phone&remember_device=true

### Resend the login code (30 s cooldown)
POST {{id}}/api/account/otp/resend
Content-Type: application/json

{ "challengeId": "PASTE_CHALLENGE_ID" }

### The signed-in user
GET {{id}}/api/account/me
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN

### Refresh ("Remember me"). Refresh tokens are one-time: use the new one each time.
POST {{id}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&client_id=mobileApp&refresh_token=PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN

### Log out (revoke the refresh token)
POST {{id}}/connect/revocation
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=mobileApp&token=PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN&token_type_hint=refresh_token

### Forgot password -> emails a code
POST {{id}}/api/account/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}" }

### Reset password (signs out all devices)
POST {{id}}/api/account/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "otp": "123456", "newPassword": "NewPassw0rd!" }

### Google / Apple: id_token from the phone. Apple also needs the raw nonce.
POST {{id}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=bmw_external&client_id=mobileApp&scope={{scope}}&provider=google&id_token=PASTE_GOOGLE_ID_TOKEN

### The token works everywhere: gateway -> auction service echoes the username
POST http://localhost:6001/auctions/test
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN
